message.content:
Review the following code diff for quality issues: redundant state, leaky abstractions, unnecessary comments, stringly-typed code, nested conditionals, parameter sprawl, copy-paste.

DIFF (code files only):

```
WorksPageRuntime.ts — _attachVideoHover() video race condition fix:
+    let isHovered = false;
+    let pendingPlay: Promise<void> | null = null;
+
+    const show = (): void => {
+      if (!isHovered) return;
+      video.style.opacity = "";
+      figure.classList.add("is-video-active");
+    };
+    const hideVideoNow = (): void => {
+      video.style.opacity = "0";
+      figure.classList.remove("is-video-active");
+    };
+    const safePause = (): void => {
+      video.pause();
+      video.currentTime = 0;
+    };
+
     const onEnter = (): void => {
+      isHovered = true;
+      video.style.opacity = "";
       if (!video.src) { video.src = videoUrl; video.load(); }
-      void video.play().catch(() => undefined);
+      pendingPlay = video.play().catch(() => undefined);
       if (video.readyState >= 3) {
         show();
       } else {
         video.addEventListener("canplay", show, { once: true });
       }
     };
     const onLeave = (): void => {
+      isHovered = false;
       video.removeEventListener("canplay", show);
-      figure.classList.remove("is-video-active");
-      video.pause();
+      hideVideoNow();
+      const p = pendingPlay;
+      pendingPlay = null;
+      if (p !== null) {
+        void p.then(() => { if (!isHovered) safePause(); });
+      } else {
+        safePause();
+      }
     };
     // cleanup:
+      isHovered = false;
       video.removeEventListener("canplay", show);
+      figure.classList.remove("is-video-active");
+      const p = pendingPlay;
+      pendingPlay = null;
+      if (p !== null) {
+        void p.then(safePause);
+      } else {
+        safePause();
+      }

WorksSceneManager.ts — snapToPosition():
+  snapToPosition(camera: THREE.Camera, targetX: number, targetY: number): void {
+    this._targetX = targetX; this._targetY = targetY;
+    this._velocityX = 0; this._velocityY = 0;
+    camera.position.x = targetX; camera.position.y = targetY;
+    camera.lookAt(targetX, targetY, 0);
+  }

usage site:
-    this.cameraMotionRuntime.setTargetPosition(center.x, center.y);
+    if (this.camera) {
+      this.cameraMotionRuntime.snapToPosition(this.camera, center.x, center.y);
+    } else {
+      this.cameraMotionRuntime.setTargetPosition(center.x, center.y);
+    }

src/Core/ImageProcessor.php — convertToWebp():
+    public const MEMORY_LIMIT = '1024M';
+    public const MAX_CONVERTIBLE_PIXELS = 16_000_000;
+    // inside makeWebpSibling: raises memory_limit, restores in finally
+    public static function convertToWebp(string $absolutePath): ?string
+    { ... calls makeWebpSibling + validates + unlinks original ... }
```

Quality checks:
1. `onLeave` cleanup block vs `_videoHoverCleanups` push block — near-identical `pendingPlay` drain logic. Is this copy-paste that should be extracted?
2. `video.style.opacity = ""` in `onEnter` AND in `show()` — double-set of the same property. Is the one in `onEnter` redundant?
3. `hideVideoNow()` sets `video.style.opacity = "0"` inline — but initial opacity=0 is SCSS-controlled. Is mixing style.opacity and SCSS opacity coherent?
4. `MEMORY_LIMIT = '1024M'` as `public const` — should this be private? It's an implementation detail of the conversion.
5. Comments in ImageProcessor.php — are they explaining WHY (constraints/invariants) or just narrating the code?

Report findings with file + line context. Under 200 words.

